!!! Creating and using a standard map from Matrix.
!!!
!!! No Matrix page in the standard library or in these tests constructed a map,
!!! so the only supported spelling was unverified and undiscoverable. An agent
!!! reading the SDK found nothing to copy, guessed
!!! 'map of text, Item.new with nothing' -- repeating the type arguments on the
!!! receiver -- and that resolved the member away, leaving a zero-argument
!!! construction of 'map' that compiled clean and failed at load time.
!!!
!!! The type arguments come from the binding's declared type; the receiver is
!!! the bare type name.
book execution.stdlib-map-construction

read everything from nil.std.core
read everything from nil.std.collections

Item begin record
    field sku as text
    field quantity as number
end record

main returns number begin paragraph
    variable stock as map of text, Item is map.new with nothing
    evaluate stock.insert with "WIDGET", (build Item with sku being "WIDGET", quantity being 12)
    evaluate stock.insert with "GEAR", (build Item with sku being "GEAR", quantity being 4)
    say (stock.length with nothing)

    consider (stock.get with "GEAR")
        when Option.Some holding found then say found.sku plus " x" plus (found.quantity becomes text)
        when Option.None then say "absent"
    end consider

    consider (stock.get with "GHOST")
        when Option.Some holding found then say found.sku
        when Option.None then say "absent"
    end consider

    give 0
end paragraph
